Character reference sheet for an original full-colour Indian slice-of-life manga. Clean confident line art with varied line weight, soft flat cel shading, warm natural light, restrained blue and teal accents, plain off-white background. Absolutely no text, letters, numbers, labels, logos or captions anywhere.

Three characters stand in three columns, each shown full body front view plus a head close-up in three-quarter view with a gentle smile, consistent proportions:

LEFT — Dr. Ananya: Indian woman in her late 30s, clinic doctor; calm, confident, caring. Teal kurta beneath an open white doctor's coat, dark leggings, flat sandals. Shoulder-length black hair tied in a low bun with a few loose strands, slim build, small gold stud earrings. Face: calm almond-shaped eyes with slightly heavy upper lids and a gentle downward outer corner; soft straight medium-thick level eyebrows; oval face with a defined slightly pointed chin and a small nose with a rounded tip. No bindi.

CENTRE — Meera: Indian woman in her late 20s, clinic receptionist; friendly and capable. Blue kurta with white churidar, thin silver bangle on her right wrist. Long black hair in a single side braid over her left shoulder, slim build. Face: large round bright eyes with a visible lower lash line; thin gently arched eyebrows set high; round face with full cheeks and a short soft chin; small dimple on the left cheek when smiling.

RIGHT — Ravi: Indian man in his mid-30s, patient; warm and approachable. Light green shirt, dark trousers, simple wristwatch on his left wrist, small dark shoulder bag. Short neat black hair with a side part, trimmed short beard, medium build. Face: warm slightly narrow eyes that crease at the outer corners when smiling; thick straight dark eyebrows close to the eyes; square jaw with a short trimmed beard and a broad nose.

Natural skin tones, precise hands, no photorealism, no glossy gradients, no surface microtexture.
